{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1546436-sorcerer-s-major-path-inheritance-questions-about-the-area-of-interest","id":1546436,"title":"Sorcerer's Major Path Inheritance - Questions about the Area of Interest","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Curseborne"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-11-26T17:58:29-08:00","id":1546436,"title":"Sorcerer's Major Path Inheritance - Questions about the Area of Interest","content":"Hello there!<br /> <br /> So my friend and I have been exploring the preview documents a lot in the past weeks, and we have come across a few questions about how to play out the &quot;Area of Interest&quot; mentioned in the Sorcerer's Major Path Inheritance.<br /> <br /> It says that the character gains hits to apply *before* the roll equal to the Entanglement on 'Appropriate Actions'.<br /> <br /> The question is, how would you rule it? My friend somewhat assumes the 'Area of Interest' should be represented by a skill, and so the hits gained would be applied to rolls pertaining to that skill. However, the wording seems to indicate that it would be just about any roll, related to it. The problem arising is that, how do you balance that then? Our understanding is that, if it was the latter option, it would be incredibly powerful!<br /> <br /> It is possible that we have missed some information on the matter, however we decided to come here and ask what the other Curseborne enthusiasts might think of that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28659,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28659-delpudding","user":"DelPudding","date":". 11-26-2024, 09:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28659-delpudding","name":"DelPudding","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-26T19:03:12-08:00","id":1546438,"title":"","content":"It seems intentionally broadly written. It could be anything from &quot;stamp collecting&quot; to &quot;necromancy&quot;.<br /> <br /> It does seem clear that it's intended to apply only to tests of *knowledge*. That is, if your area of interest was &quot;firearms&quot; you'd get the hits on rolls to know about guns, not on rolls to shoot guns.<br /> <br /> I don't think it needs to be tied to a particular skill, and I definitely don't think it should just *be* a particular skill.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}